The young priestess stepped out of the Minetown general store, unaware
it would be her last move ever.

Maybe the presence of a cockatrice, or a lizard named Emily, should
have alerted her to the fact that dangerous things were afoot.  As it
turned out, though, the presence of the bones file probably had little
to do with her demise; with an XL of 10 and an AC of -11, she and her
two large dogs were able to take on a reasonably tough monster or two.

She laughed when she saw Max and Simon roughing up a local dwarf as the
Minetown watch looked on.  Right up until the point when the desperate
dwarf pulled out his one and only possession, a prized scroll named VE
FORBRYDERNE... and filled the entire area with at least twenty
monsters.  Before the priestess could even blink, she was surrounded by
an ugly cast of characters: Two fire ants, a yeti, and an owlbear were
the worst of it.

The fire ant hits! The fire ant bites! The yeti hits! The yeti hits!
(etc.)
The owlbear grabs you!

At this point it was over.  Before she could even attempt to scrawl a
single Elbereth, her new friends had ensured her timely demise.

Ah well... another NetHack lesson reminder: "Always be prepared to host
a crowd. You never know when a horde will drop in."



